The Rust SSH tunnel (crates/tg-core/src/ssh) uses russh (Apache License, Version 2.0) with the `ring` crypto backend,
which carries ISC and OpenSSL-style licence terms (copyright Brian Smith and the OpenSSL/BoringSSL authors); its
licence text ships in the third-party licence listing of the Rust build.

The Rust MySQL driver (crates/tg-driver, feature `mysql`) uses mysql_async (MIT or Apache License, Version 2.0),
whose TLS support bundles webpki-roots: Mozilla's list of root certificates, under the Community Data License
Agreement – Permissive, Version 2.0; its licence text ships in the third-party licence listing of the Rust build.

The Rust SQL Server driver (crates/tg-driver, feature `mssql`) uses tiberius (MIT or Apache License, Version 2.0),
which links the aws-lc-rs crypto library (ISC, Apache License 2.0 and OpenSSL-style terms, copyright Amazon.com and
the OpenSSL/BoringSSL authors); TableGrip makes rustls use ring at run time, but aws-lc is compiled in.

The Rust DuckDB driver (crates/tg-driver, feature `duckdb`) builds DuckDB in (MIT License, copyright Stichting DuckDB
Foundation), which bundles third-party code under its own permissive licences, listed in DuckDB's LICENSE and
third-party notices; they ship in the third-party licence listing of the Rust build.

The Rust Redis driver (crates/tg-driver, feature `redis`) uses redis-rs (BSD 3-Clause License, copyright Armin
Ronacher and the redis-rs contributors); its licence text ships in the third-party licence listing of the Rust build.

The Rust MongoDB driver (crates/tg-driver, feature `mongodb`) uses the official mongodb and bson crates (Apache
License, Version 2.0), which bundle webpki-roots (see above) and resolve SRV records with hickory-dns (MIT or Apache
License, Version 2.0).
